Subject: cutw function resulting in output that is one sample too long when starting at t > 0
Message-ID: <MV-fy0d5EC4.i5uoWmSYCAAJ@seewave.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/seewave/c/MV-fy0d5EC4/m/i5uoWmSYCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

It looks like this issue occurs only when cutw is called with from > 0

such that
 cutw(tico, from = 0, to = 1, output = 'Wave')

gives you an output that is 1 tico-sample-rate (22050 samples) long.

However, if instead you run
cutw(tico, from = 0.5, to = 1.5, output = 'Wave')

, you get one extra sample (output is length 22051).

I believe that the error is found in the line
else a <- round(from * f)

Which should be
else a <- round(from * f) + 1

